SUSPECTED BUG: expected only sentinel dispatch.ErrMaintenance, through the
closure failWith$1 (1 of 1 candidates). Actual: no Origin, one entry
"unresolved(depends-on-caller): parameter err (error)". The parameter is
failWith's, and its caller is the Target itself (failWith(ErrMaintenance)
two lines above the dynamic call), so nothing depends on Maintenance's
caller; the label does not say whose parameter it is either.
Closure capturing an error value: failWith(err) returns a closure that
returns its free variable, and Maintenance calls the result. A closure
that captures a local of its creator works (limited_decl, e2e
dynamic/freevar_dynamic). ErrRateLimited (the other returned closure,
Limit$1) must be absent, and is.
